  "name": null,
  "problem": "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed by the curves $y={x}^{2}$ and $y=-x+2.$ If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+xy, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,{∬}_{D}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}+xy)\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of the rectangular domain $R?$\n\nI. $R=[-2,1]\\times [-1,2]$\n\nII. $R=[-3,2]\\times [-1,4]$\n\nIII. $R=[-3,1]\\times [2,4]$",
